[{:adr/authoritative_for ["cloud-itonami-isic-0240 support-services-to-forestry forestry-support-service operations coordination actor implementation" "fresh scaffold closing the kotoba-lang/industry placeholder gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0240 gap"], :adr/topic "cloud-itonami-isic-0240-forestry-support-services-coverage", :adr/related ["cloud-itonami-isic-0161"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2613100000-cloud-itonami-isic-0240-forestry-support-services-coverage", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-16", :adr/body "# ADR-2613100000: cloud-itonami-isic-0240 (Support services to forestry) forestry-support-service operations-coordination actor -- fresh scaffold, full implementation

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-16
**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)
**Related**: cloud-itonami-isic-0161 (Support activities for crop
production -- the reference module shape this actor mirrors, independently
re-read in full before use), the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry's
`\"0240\"` catalog entry (previously `:spec` with a placeholder
`gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0240` repo link that was never populated)

## Context

`kotoba-lang/industry`'s registry carried a `\"0240\"` entry at `:maturity
:spec` pointing at `https://github.com/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0240` -- a
placeholder repo link with no actual implementation behind it (no source,
no tests; confirmed 404 via `gh api` for both the placeholder and the real
`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0240` before any work began). This is
part of an ongoing careful, smaller-batch rollout (one ISIC class per
agent, a capable model, mandatory verification) after a prior 18-agent
haiku batch produced a 61% defect rate on other ISIC classes; 138+
consecutive agents on this stricter protocol had all succeeded since. This
ADR covers ISIC 0240 only. Before any work began, the registry entry's
identity (`{:id \"0240\" :name \"Support services to forestry\"}`) was
independently verified against a fresh clone of `kotoba-lang/industry`,
per this fleet's caution against ID/name mismatches (prior agents in this
fleet had mislabeled other ISIC classes) -- confirmed correct, no
mismatch. ISIC 0240 covers CONTRACT LOGGING-SUPPORT SERVICES: cruising
(timber-resource survey), forest-fire-protection support, seed collection,
and transport of logs within the forest -- distinct from actual timber
harvesting (felling) itself, which sits in ISIC's timber-harvesting
divisions (022x).

## Decision

Scaffold `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0240` as a forestry-SUPPORT-
SERVICE OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor (not direct forestry-equipment
operation authority, not a fire-suppression-tactics authority), mirroring
`cloud-itonami-isic-0161`'s verified module shape
(`facts`/`registry`/`store`/`governor`/`operation`/`phase`/`advisor`/
`sim`, `deps.edn`/`blueprint.edn`/README/GOVERNANCE/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/
CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY) with fresh, forestry-support-service-specific
domain logic under the `forestrysupport` namespace. ISIC 0240 covers
CONTRACT logging-support work performed for OTHER forest operators on a
fee/contract basis -- the operator never fells or owns the standing
timber being serviced, which is what distinguishes this actor from the
actual timber-harvesting divisions (022x) themselves, which drives every
domain-specific check below:

1. **`forestrysupport.facts`** -- service-type safety windows split
   across survey/collection service types (timber cruising, seed
   collection -- no field-equipment-operation safety window at all,
   `nil` for operator-certification/equipment-inspection/wind-speed/
   riparian-buffer/load-limit fields) and field-equipment-operation
   service types (forest-fire-protection support patrol-and-fuelbreak-
   maintenance, in-forest log transport -- each with a genuine
   operator-certification requirement, an equipment-inspection interval,
   and -- where physically applicable to that specific service -- a
   maximum fieldwork wind speed, a minimum riparian buffer, and a
   maximum haul-road load), plus jurisdiction evidence-checklist
   requirements (JP 森林法・林野庁 / US State Forest Practices Act / CA
   British Columbia FRPA). Not every field-equipment-operation service
   type carries every physical-constraint field -- in-forest log-haul
   has no fieldwork wind-speed ceiling of its own (haul-road travel is
   not wind-sensitive the way canopy-adjacent chainsaw fuel-break work
   is) and fire-protection-support patrol/fuel-break work carries no
   haul-road load limit (it hauls no logs) -- the Governor's
   corresponding check is skipped entirely, never fabricated, when a
   given service type's field is nil.
2. **`forestrysupport.registry`** -- pure, host-clock-free validation
   predicates the Governor uses to independently verify physical/
   regulatory constraints: operator-certification expiry,
   equipment-inspection overdue (per-type interval, not a single
   hardcoded window -- fire-protection-support's 30-day interval is
   stricter than log-transport's 60-day interval, a genuine domain
   difference caught while writing the tests), wind-speed exceeded,
   riparian-buffer violated, and load-limit exceeded.
3. **`forestrysupport.store`** -- plain-data store (`{:service-orders
   {...} :facts [...]}`) with service-order lookup/registration/logged/
   scheduled flags and an append-only audit ledger.
4. **`forestrysupport.governor`** -- 13 independently-verified
   hard-violation checks plus a closed operation allowlist as a hard,
   permanent block per the domain design: the advisor may only ever
   propose `:log-service-record`, `:schedule-field-operation`,
   `:flag-forest-health-concern`, `:order-supplies` (all `:effect
   :propose`); anything else -- most importantly direct
   chainsaw/skidder/patrol-vehicle control -- is refused unconditionally
   (`:op-not-allowed`), never a soft escalation. A dedicated
   `:forestry-equipment-or-fire-tactic-decision-blocked` check adds
   defense-in-depth against a proposal that covertly requests direct
   forestry-equipment control or a final fire-suppression-tactic
   decision via a marker nested inside an otherwise-allowed op's
   `:value` -- evaluated unconditionally against every op, a permanent
   block never overridable by human approval, matching this fleet's
   established pattern of structural (not merely documented) scope
   boundaries. The `:service-order-not-registered` invariant is applied
   across ALL FOUR allowed ops, per this actor's explicit domain-design
   requirement that a service-order/client-forest-operator record be
   independently verified/registered before any action at all.
   `:flag-forest-health-concern` always escalates to a human regardless
   of confidence, as does `:log-service-record` (the one real actuation
   event this actor performs); `:order-supplies` above a 5000 USD cost
   threshold (`governor/supply-order-cost-threshold-usd`) likewise
   always escalates, while at or below the threshold it may auto-commit
   when the Governor is otherwise clean.
5. **`forestrysupport.phase`** -- `:intake -> :survey -> :advise ->
   :treat -> :record -> :audit`. This sequence was NOT invented fresh: it
   is the registry's own already-registered `:operating-states` for
   `\"0240\"` (present since the entry's original `:spec` placeholder, and
   identical to `\"0161\"`'s own sequence), confirmed meaningful (not a
   placeholder sequence) and adopted verbatim rather than overwritten.
   Uses the same portable `keep-indexed`-based `index-of` helper 0161
   established (not the JVM-only `.indexOf`), so this actor ships
   cljs-portable from day one.
6. **`deps.edn` / `blueprint.edn` / docs** -- mirror
   `cloud-itonami-isic-0161`'s shape (`:test`/`:lint`/`:run`/`:dev`
   aliases, `itonami.blueprint/*` metadata, scope/design/testing README
   sections). `:itonami.blueprint/robotics` is honestly `false` (this
   actor holds no chainsaw/skidder/patrol-vehicle-control authority).

### What this actor does NOT do

Operating a chainsaw, skidder, or patrol vehicle remains exclusive to the
licensed field-equipment operator in the field, permanently, with no actor
or human-approval override path -- enforced structurally by both the
closed operation allowlist and the dedicated
`forestry-equipment-or-fire-tactic-decision-blocked` defense-in-depth
check, not just documented. This actor also does not finalize a
fire-suppression-tactic decision on its own (same permanent block), and
does not fell or otherwise harvest timber -- that is ISIC's
timber-harvesting divisions (022x), out of scope entirely.

