## Consequences

(+) `cloud-itonami-isic-0240` now has a real, tested implementation
matching the shape of every other cloud-itonami ISIC actor, replacing a
placeholder registry entry that pointed at a repo that never existed.
(+) `kotoba-lang/industry` registry `\"0240\"` entry promoted to `:maturity
:implemented`.
(+) `forestrysupport.facts`/`forestrysupport.governor`'s asymmetric
per-service-type `nil`-guarded physical-constraint checks (not every
field-equipment-operation service type carries every one of
wind-speed/riparian-buffer/load-limit) extend the pattern
`cloud-itonami-isic-0170` established for trap-vs-direct-take harvest
methods to a third distinct shape: within a single \"field-equipment-
operation\" category, individual physical-constraint fields can still be
genuinely inapplicable to a specific service type, not just to an entire
category -- a reusable pattern for any future ISIC class in this fleet's
agriculture/forestry/fishing cluster with this finer-grained shape.
(+) The per-service-type equipment-inspection interval (30 days for
fire-protection-support vs. 60 days for log-haul, rather than a single
hardcoded window) demonstrates a genuine domain difference the tests
caught during development, distinct from 0161's single fixed 90-day
sprayer-calibration window.
(-) `forestrysupport.advisor` remains a documentation-only stub (no
`MockAdvisor` implementation); `forestrysupport.operation/run-operation`
takes an already-formed proposal plus an injected `governor-fn` rather
than internally invoking an advisor. This matches
`cloud-itonami-isic-0161`'s own current shape and is a natural, contained
future extension, not required for this ADR's verification bar.
